e stable baseline. The files under `startup-patches/` are also\\n+captured for discovery, but must not be applied to the stable baseline unless\\n+their features are deliberately selected.\\n+\\n+## Important environment facts\\n+\\n+- Container image: `tiered-serve:latest`, Linux ARM64, imported single-layer\\n+  rootfs rather than a Dockerfile build.\\n+- Container OS: Ubuntu 24.04.4.\\n+- Python runtime: 3.12.3 from `tiered-serve/.venv`.\\n+- PyTorch: `2.11.0a0+git70d99e9`, built with CUDA 13.2 for `sm_90`.\\n+- vLLM: `0.13.1.dev0+g72506c983.d20260406`.\\n+- GCC: 13.3.0.\\n+- CMake: no system command; venv CMake is 3.31.10.\\n+- Full `uv pip freeze`: `manifests/uv-pip-freeze.txt` (175 entries).\\n+- Full Debian package inventory: `manifests/dpkg-query.txt`.\\n+\\n+The stable `build.sh` requests Python 3.11 and CUDA-12 cuDNN packages, while\\n+the observed runtime is Python 3.12/CUDA 13.2. Treat the observed manifests as\\n+the environment of record and the old build script as source material, not as\\n+a byte-for-byte reproduction recipe.\\n+\\n+The freeze contains a stale editable entry for\\n+`/root/projects/LLM-bitfield-compressor`, but that path does not exist in the\\n+captured container. This dependency must be resolved or removed in the new\\n+build.\\n+\\n+## CUDA 13.2 forward-compatibility resolution\\n+\\n+The host driver reports 580.105.08 / CUDA 13.0, but the process actually loads:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+/usr/local/cuda-13.2/compat/libcuda.so.595.45.04\\n+/usr/local/cuda-13.2/targets/sbsa-linux/lib/libcudart.so.13.2.51\\n+```\\n+\\n+The installed compatibility package is `cuda-compat-13-2` version\\n+`595.45.04-1ubuntu1`. See `manifests/cuda-compat-*` and\\n+`manifests/cuda-library-paths.txt`.\\n+\\n+## Patch application order\\n+\\n+Starting from clean checkouts at the pinned commits:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git -C /root/projects/vllm apply --check \\\\\\n+  /root/projects/tiered-serve/patches/vllm.patch\\n+git -C /root/projects/vllm apply \\\\\\n+  /root/projects/tiered-serve/patches/vllm.patch\\n+\\n+git -C /root/projects/vllm-flash-attn apply --check \\\\\\n+  /root/projects/tiered-serve/patches/vllm-flash-attn.patch\\n+git -C /root/projects/vllm-flash-attn apply \\\\\\n+  /root/projects/tiered-serve/patches/vllm-flash-attn.patch\\n+\\n+git -C /root/projects/pytorch apply --check \\\\\\n+  /root/projects/tiered-serve/patches/pytorch.patch\\n+git -C /root/projects/pytorch apply \\\\\\n+  /root/projects/tiered-serve/patches/pytorch.patch\\n+```\\n+\\n+All native artifacts must be rebuilt for x86-64/Blackwell. Do not copy the\\n+ARM64 venv, `.so` files, Torch extension cache, or compiled objects.\\n+\\n+## Launch material\\n+\\n+- `scripts/host/`: host orchestration script and its `model_map.sh` dependency.\\n+- `scripts/container/`: container copies of `run_experiment*.sh`, model map, and\\n+  Azure-conversation client.\\n+- `config/cao-p4-kvcomp.yaml`: exact runtime layout configuration.\\n+- `startup-patches/`: every text patch mounted at\\n+  `/opt/tiered-serve-startup-patches`.\\n+\\n+The host and container copies of `run_experiment_tmux.sh` differ; checksums are\\n+in `metadata/scripts.sha256`.\\n+\\n+The successful historical server command expanded by the host script was:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+LD_PRELOAD=/root/projects/tiered-serve/etc/stack_pool.so \\\\\\n+numactl -m 0 python serve_offload_kvweight.py \\\\\\n+  --model meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct \\\\\\n+  --weight-comp p4flat \\\\\\n+  --fused-mm \\\\\\n+  --kv-comp p4flat \\\\\\n+  --ts-configs cao-p4-kvcomp\\n+```\\n+\\n+`python` assumed an already activated TieredServe venv. Use the explicit venv\\n+path in a new build.\\n+\\n+Historical performance client command:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+taskset -c 7 bash scripts/serving/client/azure_conv.sh \\\\\\n+  llama70b cao-p4-kvcomp\\n+```\\n+\\n+The corresponding trace is\\n+`validation/AzureLLMInferenceTrace_conv_sample_1200.csv`; its SHA-256 is in\\n+`validation/trace-files.sha256`.\\n+\\n+## Validation status\\n+\\n+No clean stable acceptance run was performed during bundle generation. Doing\\n+that correctly requires isolated clean checkouts with the committed patches\\n+and rebuilt native extensions. Reusing the current editable venv would silently\\n+import dirty sources and would not prove stable reproduction.\\n+\\n+Files prefixed `historical-dirty-` are evidence from earlier dirty working-tree\\n+runs only. They show:\\n+\\n+- a successful API startup and request-processing run on 2026-08-21;\\n+- a six-case 70B feature matrix with identical generated token IDs\\n+  `[[60704, 13]]` and SHA-256\\n+  `803b3ce77849060dd4908990abdd60c491995f59b46dbe533e3bfd2bdf4a1340`.\\n+\\n+They are not the final stable acceptance oracle.\\n+\\n+For a future clean run, pin model and tokenizer to the immutable revision in\\n+`validation/model-tokenizer-revision.txt`, use\\n+`validation/staged_correctness_prompt.txt`, and preserve:\\n+\\n+1. generated token artifact and semantic `Paris` check;\\n+2. successful `/health` response;\\n+3. GPU/LPDDR allocation and routing lines;\\n+4. explicit model and tokenizer revision;\\n+5. client command and trace SHA-256 when measuring performance.\\n+\\n+## Checksums\\n+\\n+`SHA256SUMS` covers every payload file except itself. Verify after extraction:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS\\n+```\\n*** Add File: gh200-stable-repro-discovery-20260831.42QXQx/metadata/equivalent-container-run.sh\\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n+# Semantically reconstructed from Docker inspect; the original CLI string was\\n+# not present in shell history.\\n+docker run -dit \\\\\\n+  --name tiered-serve \\\\\\n+  --gpus all \\\\\\n+  --privileged \\\\\\n+  --cap-add IPC_LOCK \\\\\\n+  --security-opt label=disable \\\\\\n+  --shm-size 480g \\\\\\n+  -p 23456:22 \\\\\\n+  -v /lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve:/opt/tiered-serve-startup-patches:ro \\\\\\n+  -v /lambda/nfs/whchoi/github-ssh:/opt/persistent-github-ssh:ro \\\\\\n+  -v /mnt/hugepages:/mnt/hugepages \\\\\\n+  tiered-serve /bin/bash\\n*** Add File: gh200-stable-repro-discovery-20260831.42QXQx/validation/VALIDATION_STATUS.md\\n+# Stable validation status\\n+\\n+Status: **not executed**.\\n+\\n+The current container uses dirty editable source trees. A clean stable run was\\n+not launched because that would require isolated clean checkouts and rebuilding\\n+all CUDA/native extensions. Running the current venv against a partial clean\\n+checkout would not be a valid stable baseline.\\n+\\n+The included `historical-dirty-*` files are reference evidence only. The final\\n+acceptance run must use the commits in the bundle README, the committed patches\\n+in `stable-patches/`, and an explicitly pinned model/tokenizer revision.\\n+\\n+Required acceptance evidence:\\n+\\n+- fixed prompt: `staged_correctness_prompt.txt`;\\n+- semantic answer contains `Paris`;\\n+- generated token IDs and SHA-256;\\n+- HTTP `/health` success;\\n+- model/tokenizer revision;\\n+- GPU/LPDDR layout and routing log lines;\\n+- exact client command and trace SHA-256 for performance runs.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0570a-0a07-7960-a515-846514f6040a","create_time":1788166919.945528}}}
